  "caveats": {
    "masking": "aligned and random cells are applied by masking, which keeps every weight and matmul and so measures accuracy retention only. Under --uniform-per-layer the same two sets are additionally applied by slice_heads() (sliced_aligned / sliced_random_mean), which is what turns the retention into a real size reduction. Without the flag SAL's set is not uniform per layer and cannot be sliced at all.",
    "sliced_random_draws": "the sliced random cell uses a quarter of the draws, since each one rebuilds the model.",
    "int4": "per-output-channel symmetric weight round-trip on every nn.Linear except the classifier, as in the prototype.",
    "drophead_aligned": "drophead never had a pruned set of its own; it is scored on SAL's set so every arm faces the same perturbation."
  },
